### Script Node Config Schema

```typescript
interface ScriptNodeConfig {
  // Format
  archetype: string;
  targetDuration: string;
  
  // Structure
  sections: Section[];
  
  // Hook
  hookSource: 'saved' | 'examples' | 'fresh';
  hookContentId?: string;        // If saved
  hookTag?: string;              // If using @tag
  hookExampleTags?: string[];    // If examples
  hookStyles?: string[];         // If fresh
  hookCount?: number;            // If fresh
  
  // Title
  titleSource: 'saved' | 'examples' | 'fresh';
  titleContentId?: string;
  titleTag?: string;
  titleExampleTags?: string[];
  titleCount?: number;
  
  // Description
  descriptionSource: 'saved' | 'template' | 'fresh';
  descriptionContentId?: string;
  descriptionTag?: string;
  descriptionTemplate?: string;
  
  // AI
  model: string;
  temperature: number;
  customInstructions?: string;
}
```

### Runtime Behavior

**Hook Resolution:**
```
If hookSource = 'saved':
  1. Fetch by hookContentId OR resolve hookTag via /api/content/resolve
  2. Return exact content as hook
  
If hookSource = 'examples':
  1. Resolve hookExampleTags to get example hooks
  2. Include in AI prompt: "Match the style of these examples: ..."
  3. Generate new hook
  
If hookSource = 'fresh':
  1. Generate hookCount hooks with hookStyles preferences
  2. Auto-select best one (or let AI pick)
```

Same pattern for title and description.

